From 2a34cdcc8ba4fbe3af73c9ad827491dbb0d98c82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: askimi <44218719+RNI4114@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 21:00:59 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 08/21] vulkan/bvh: morton sort: spin on a relaxed RMW instead
 of an acquire load

An acquire load at device scope is a full L1 invalidate per spin iteration on
Xe2, which also throws away the cached data of the workgroups still merging
on the same core. Spin relaxed and rely on the acquire barrier after the
loop. A relaxed atomic load may be served from a stale cache line (the
counter left full by the previous build), so the spin uses atomicAdd(0).

TLAS of 43.4k instances on a B580: sort 186 -> 169 us.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 0c2d76aa4d30fa3235343f0182a33d2cffc62515)
(cherry picked from commit f8542ceb739892d85870cf21058dfcb32eba61d7)
---
 src/vulkan/runtime/bvh/morton_sort.comp | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/vulkan/runtime/bvh/morton_sort.comp b/src/vulkan/runtime/bvh/morton_sort.comp
index 0db8fef5974..2ea094c4f94 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/runtime/bvh/morton_sort.comp
+++ b/src/vulkan/runtime/bvh/morton_sort.comp
@@ -605,11 +605,15 @@ main()
          continue;
       }
 
-      /* Spin waiting for outstanding work to finish. */
+      /* Spin waiting for outstanding work to finish. The spin is relaxed: the acquire barrier below
+       * synchronizes once it exits. An acquire in the loop is a full L1 invalidate per iteration on
+       * some GPUs (Xe2), which also throws away the cached data of the workgroups still merging on
+       * the same core. A read-modify-write is used because a relaxed atomic load may be served from
+       * a stale cache line (e.g. the counter left full by a previous build).
+       */
       if (gl_LocalInvocationID.x == 0) {
-         while (atomicLoad(DEREF(INDEX(morton_ready_count, args.counts, log2_multiplier - 1)).done, gl_ScopeDevice,
-                           gl_StorageSemanticsBuffer,
-                           gl_SemanticsAcquire | gl_SemanticsMakeVisible) < gl_NumWorkGroups.x) {}
+         while (atomicAdd(DEREF(INDEX(morton_ready_count, args.counts, log2_multiplier - 1)).done, 0, gl_ScopeDevice,
+                          0, gl_SemanticsRelaxed) < gl_NumWorkGroups.x) {}
       }
 
       barrier();
